    "content": "{\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"content\": \"#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <string.h>\\n#include <math.h>\\n\\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\\n\\n/* Block sizes for tiling */\\n#define IBLOCK 4\\n#define JBLOCK 128\\n\\n/* Structure-of-Arrays layout: separate arrays per coordinate/velocity component.\\n   The original binary format uses interleaved (AoS) order, so we convert at I/O. */\\ntypedef struct {\\n    float *x, *y, *z;\\n    float *vx, *vy, *vz;\\n} SoABodies;\\n\\n/* Allocate aligned memory for a single component array of n floats */\\nstatic float* alloc_float_array(int n) {\\n    void *ptr = NULL;\\n    if (posix_memalign(&ptr, 64, n * sizeof(float)) != 0) {\\n        fprintf(stderr, \\\"Memory allocation failed\\\\n\\\");\\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n    }\\n    return (float*)ptr;\\n}\\n\\n/* Convert from AoS (Body array) to SoA */\\nstatic void aos_to_soa(const float *aos, int n, SoABodies *soa) {\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\\n        soa->x[i] = aos[6*i + 0];\\n        soa->y[i] = aos[6*i + 1];\\n        soa->z[i] = aos[6*i + 2];\\n        soa->vx[i] = aos[6*i + 3];\\n        soa->vy[i] = aos[6*i + 4];\\n        soa->vz[i] = aos[6*i + 5];\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/* Convert from SoA to AoS (Body array) */\\nstatic void soa_to_aos(const SoABodies *soa, int n, float *aos) {\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\\n        aos[6*i + 0] = soa->x[i];\\n        aos[6*i + 1] = soa->y[i];\\n        aos[6*i + 2] = soa->z[i];\\n        aos[6*i + 3] = soa->vx[i];\\n        aos[6*i + 4] = soa->vy[i];\\n        aos[6*i + 5] = soa->vz[i];\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/* Compute gravitational forces using tiled loops and SoA layout.\\n   The inner j-loop is blocked to reuse loaded body coordinates across multiple i bodies.\\n   Accumulation order per body remains sequential (j from 0..n-1) because blocks are processed in increasing order. */\\nvoid body_force(SoABodies *p, float dt, int n) {\\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\\n    for (int i_block = 0; i_block < n; i_block += IBLOCK) {\\n        int i_end = i_block + IBLOCK;\\n        if (i_end > n) i_end = n;\\n\\n        /* Local accumulators for each body in the current i-block */\\n        float fx[IBLOCK], fy[IBLOCK], fz[IBLOCK];\\n        for (int ii = 0; ii < i_end - i_block; ++ii) {\\n            fx[ii] = 0.0f;\\n            fy[ii] = 0.0f;\\n            fz[ii] = 0.0f;\\n        }\\n\\n        /* Loop over j in blocks */\\n        for (int j_block = 0; j_block < n; j_block += JBLOCK) {\\n            int j_end = j_block + JBLOCK;\\n            if (j_end > n) j_end = n;\\n\\n            /* Process each body j within the current j-block */\\n            for (int j = j_block; j < j_end; ++j) {\\n                float pjx = p->x[j];\\n                float pjy = p->y[j];\\n                float pjz = p->z[j];\\n\\n                /* Accumulate contributions to all i bodies in the current i-block */\\n                for (int ii = 0; ii < i_end - i_block; ++ii) {\\n                    int i = i_block + ii;\\n                    float dx = pjx - p->x[i];\\n                    float dy = pjy - p->y[i];\\n                    float dz = pjz - p->z[i];\\n                    float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\\n                    float inv_dist = 1.0f / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\\n                    float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\\n\\n                    fx[ii] += dx * inv_dist3;\\n                    fy[ii] += dy * inv_dist3;\\n                    fz[ii] += dz * inv_dist3;\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        /* Update velocities for bodies in this i-block */\\n        for (int ii = 0; ii < i_end - i_block; ++ii) {\\n            int i = i_block + ii;\\n            p->vx[i] += dt * fx[ii];\\n            p->vy[i] += dt * fy[ii];\\n            p->vz[i] += dt * fz[ii];\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/* Read binary dataset, convert to SoA internally */\\nSoABodies read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\\n    int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\\n    if (b != 1) {\\n        fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError reading nbodie value\\\\n\\\");\\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n    }\\n\\n    int n = *nbodies;\\n    /* Temporary AoS buffer for I/O */\\n    float *aos_buf = (float*)malloc(n * 6 * sizeof(float));\\n    if (!aos_buf) {\\n        fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nMemory allocation failed\\\\n\\\");\\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n    }\\n\\n    b = fread(aos_buf, n * 6 * sizeof(float), 1, stdin);\\n    if (b != 1) {\\n        fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError reading input values\\\\n\\\");\\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n    }\\n\\n    SoABodies soa;\\n    soa.x = alloc_float_array(n);\\n    soa.y = alloc_float_array(n);\\n    soa.z = alloc_float_array(n);\\n    soa.vx = alloc_float_array(n);\\n    soa.vy = alloc_float_array(n);\\n    soa.vz = alloc_float_array(n);\\n\\n    aos_to_soa(aos_buf, n, &soa);\\n    free(aos_buf);\\n\\n    return soa;\\n}\\n\\n/* Write SoA back to binary AoS format */\\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, const SoABodies *bodies) {\\n    float *aos_buf = (float*)malloc(nbodies * 6 * sizeof(float));\\n    if (!aos_buf) {\\n        fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nMemory allocation failed\\\\n\\\");\\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n    }\\n\\n    soa_to_aos(bodies, nbodies, aos_buf);\\n\\n    int b = fwrite(aos_buf, nbodies * 6 * sizeof(float), 1, stdout);\\n    if (b != 1) {\\n        fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError writing to output\\\\n\\\");\\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n    }\\n\\n    free(aos_buf);\\n}\\n\\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\\n    int nbodies;\\n\\n    SoABodies bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\\n\\n    /* Simulation iterations */\\n    for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; iter++) {\\n        body_force(&bodies, DT, nbodies);\\n\\n        /* Update positions using velocities */\\n        #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\\n        for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; i++) {\\n            bodies.x[i] += bodies.vx[i] * DT;\\n            bodies.y[i] += bodies.vy[i] * DT;\\n            bodies.z[i] += bodies.vz[i] * DT;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    write_dataset(nbodies, &bodies);\\n\\n    free(bodies.x);\\n    free(bodies.y);\\n    free(bodies.z);\\n    free(bodies.vx);\\n    free(bodies.vy);\\n    free(bodies.vz);\\n\\n    exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\\n}\\n\",\n      \"path\": \"src/nbody.c\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Tiling both the outer i-loop and inner j-loop (i-block size 4, j-block size 128) combined with Structure-of-Arrays data layout improves memory locality by reusing each loaded body coordinate across multiple bodies in a tile. The accumulation order per body remains sequential because j-blocks are processed in increasing index order and within each block j increases; thus floating-point operations occur in exactly the same sequence as the original, preserving bit-exact results. OpenMP parallelization over i-blocks exploits all 4 cores without changing per-body computation order.\",\n  \"notes\": \"The transformation uses compile-time constant block sizes to avoid VLA issues. I/O conversion between AoS and SoA adds overhead but is expected to be outweighed by better cache behavior during the O(n^2) force calculation. The inner loop loads each body j's coordinates once per i-block, reducing memory traffic compared to loading them for every single i.\",\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Structure-of-Arrays (SoA) data layout\",\n    \"Loop tiling on both outer and inner loops with fixed block sizes\",\n    \"OpenMP parallelization over i-blocks\"\n  ]\n}",
